From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:30:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Declare where miclow states the same thing twice, and
 what is right

pw-facts.json lists seven things miclow states in more than one place
(its version, licence, the task id variable, the system commands, the
task configuration keys, the Python client's methods, the repository
URL) and where each is stated. pw-log.jsonl is the record of how each
place was read; pw-calibration.json the measurement of the readers.

Three of them disagree. For those, what is right is laid down: the
licence is MIT, as in LICENSE; the configuration keys and the client's
methods are what the code has.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016CDHSwZWzVoy1TC6nxh6gX
